The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says the reports are one issue with one fix queued. Its own
table shows more than one cause. Read report by report, #4471 holds three problems. Each one has
a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 closed on 5 October: the parser is fixed and the booking-v3 form is retired. The one-day
move is not touched by either change. Its ticket stays open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| problem | in the table above | ticket | after #4471 closed |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` — day and month swapped | the `parser` row | [#1](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/1) | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` — booking-v3 form asks month first | the `hint` row | [#2](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/2) | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired |
| `one-day move` — date lands one day off | the note under the table, counted within `parser` | [#3](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/3) | open |

## The three problems

**`parser` — day and month swapped.** The shared parser read every date month first. Every
tenant on file writes the day first, so 3 May became 5 March. Engineering fixed it when #4471
closed. Ticket [#1](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/1), closed.

**`hint` — the booking-v3 form asks for the wrong order.** Under its date field, booking-v3
printed `MM/DD/YYYY`. People typed month first, as the hint told them, and the form read the
tenant's way, day first. Only form reports from tenants on booking-v3. The parser fix did not
touch it; the form is retired instead, so no fix is coming. Ticket
[#2](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/2), closed as won't fix.

**`one-day move` — the date lands one day off.** These reports describe a date one day early,
an invite sent before the booking, and two clients in Lisbon and Toronto who got different days
for one meeting. That is a time zone problem, not a swap. The desk noted them
(`desk-notes.json`) and files them under `parser` by tenant, so the table counts them there. The
parser fix does not close them. Ticket [#3](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/3),
open.

## How the count was made

- The export repeats some rows. One id is one report.
- Cause by tenant and channel, as in `causes.ts`. `intakeTag` is not the cause: intake tags
  `hint` whenever the reporter's browser is `en-US`.
- Each ticket counts its reports the desk's way, as the table above shows them.

## What changes on the desk

- Merging on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put all three
  problems in one ticket, because their subjects match. Check the cause before you merge.
- New one-day reports after 5 October go to #3, not to the parser.

